.TH MAKE-DATA-DIRS.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
make\-data\-dirs.py \- create the /<area>/<run type>/<subsystem>/ data directory tree on a DAQ node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 bin/make\-data\-dirs.py
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates, with
.BR "os.makedirs(..., exist_ok=True)" ,
every directory
.RI / area / runtype / subsystem /
for
.TP
.I area
.BR data ,
.BR data\-2 ,
.BR test\-data ,
.B scratch
.TP
.I runtype
.BR test ,
.BR prod ,
.BR commissioning ,
.BR study ,
.B other
.TP
.I subsystem
.BR calo ,
.BR trk ,
.BR crv ,
.BR stm ,
.BR extmon ,
.BR aux ,
.B other
.PP
140 directories, printing one line per directory.
The lists are fixed in the script.
Creating top\-level directories needs root.
.PP
No other package in the suite creates or reads this layout (searched
2026\-10\-06), so whether it is still the cluster convention is not
established here.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.RI / area / runtype / subsystem /
as above.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 0; a directory that cannot be created is reported on stdout and
skipped.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
sudo python3 bin/make\-data\-dirs.py
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkdir (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
